Fixes to nju-websoft/KG-ICL at 6a3166e347ae468acdfb30a70a2cf3608b66b8f1; apply with
patch -p1 in the checkout root. It changes only the defects documented in docs/kgicl.md:

B1 src/encoder/EntityEncoder.py: the attention activation was a fresh nn.RReLU(), which is
   always in training mode, so inference sampled random negative slopes. Use the module's
   training flag: random slopes in training, the mean slope in evaluation.
B2 src/data_loader.py: evaluation slot i of the batch-wide relation list selected case i mod
   n_cases, which depends on the relation's rank among the batch relations when it has fewer
   than shot cases. Select case (i mod shot) mod n_cases.
B3 run_your_own_dataset/utils_all.py: distance labels were paired with prompt nodes in set
   iteration order and the loader reads label rows as local node IDs, so most entities got
   another entity's tokens. Pair each node with its own label, rows in local-ID order.
B4 run_your_own_dataset/utils_all.py: a self-loop pair was looked up in both directions,
   duplicating its facts in the prompt graph.
B5 src/data_loader.py: for a self-loop example fact (u, q, u) the tail token went to local
   node 1, an unrelated entity. Both tokens go to the example entity.

